[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Man-made Disease]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.59]Lesson 17 | 第17课
[00:02.78]A man-made disease | 人为的疾病
[00:11.76]What factor helped to spread the disease of myxomatosis? | 什么因素助长了多发性粘液瘤病的传播？
[00:18.28]In the early days of the settlement of Australia, enterprising settlers unwisely introduced the European rabbit. | 在澳大利亚移民定居的早期，富有开拓精神的移民不明智地引进了欧洲的兔子。
[00:28.42]This rabbit had no natural enemies in the Antipodes, so that it multiplied with that promiscuous abandon characteristic of rabbits. | 这种兔子在澳大利亚没有天敌，因此便以兔子所特有的那种放肆的杂交繁衍大量增加起来。
[00:40.42]It overran a whole continent. | 它遍布整个大陆。
[00:43.87]It caused devastation by burrowing and by devouring the herbage which might have maintained millions of sheep and cattle. | 它靠打洞和吞食可能养活数百万头牛羊的牧草而造成了毁灭性的破坏。
[00:52.99]Scientists discovered that this particular variety of rabbit (and apparently no other animal) was susceptible to a fatal virus disease, myxomatosis. | 科学家们发现，这种兔子（显然再没有别的动物）易患一种致命的病毒性疾病，即多发性粘液瘤。
[01:06.84]By infecting animals and letting them loose in the burrows, local epidemics of this disease could be created. | 通过感染这种动物并把它们放进洞穴，当地就能造成这种疾病的流行。
[01:15.06]Later it was found that there was a type of mosquito which acted as the carrier of this disease and passed it on to the rabbits. | 后来发现有一种蚊子是这种疾病的携带者，能把它传染给兔子。
[01:23.84]So while the rest of the world was trying to get rid of mosquitoes, Australia was encouraging this one. | 因此，当世界上其他地方都在努力消灭蚊子时，澳大利亚却在助长这种蚊子的繁殖。
[01:31.14]It effectively spread the disease all over the continent and drastically reduced the rabit population. | 它有效地把疾病传播到整个大陆，并急剧地减少了兔子的数量。
[01:39.62]It later became apparent that rabbits were developing a degree of resistance to this disease, | 后来才弄清楚，兔子对这种疾病逐渐产生了一定的抵抗力，
[01:45.88]so that the rabbit population was unlikely to be completely exterminated. | 因此兔子的数量不太可能被完全消灭。
[01:51.88]There were hopes, however, that the problem of the rabbit would become manageable. | 然而，人们希望兔子问题变得可以控制。
[01:58.72]Ironically, Europe, which had bequeathed the rabbit as a pest to Australia, acquired this man-made disease as a pestilence. | 具有讽刺意味的是，把兔子作为害兽传给澳大利亚的欧洲，自己却染上了这种人为的疾病，如同一场瘟疫。
[02:09.37]A French physician decided to get rid of the wild rabbits on his own estate and introduced myxomatosis. | 一位法国医生决定除掉自己庄园里的野兔，便引进了多发性粘液瘤病。
[02:17.03]It did not, however, remain within the confines of this estate. | 然而，这种疾病并没有被限制在那个庄园的范围之内。
[02:22.13]It spread through France, where wild rabbits are not generally regarded as a pest but as a sport and a useful food supply, | 它传遍了法国，而法国的野兔一般不被当作害兽，而被当作猎物和有用的食物来源，
[02:31.53]and it spread to Britain where wild rabbits are regarded as a pest but where domesticated rabbits, | 它还传到了英国，那里的野兔虽然被当作害兽，可是家兔，
[02:38.62]equally susceptible to the disease, are the basis of a profitable fur industry. | 同样容易感染这种疾病，却是一项有利可图的毛皮工业的基础。
[02:45.50]The question became one of whether Man could control the disease he had invented. | 于是问题变成了：人能否控制住他自己发明的这种疾病。
